 ## What you get
 
 - **Floating orb** — a smoked-glass instrument with a 36-segment LED gauge. As speed climbs, so does its title — from *Walking* and *Bicycle* through *Bullet Train* and *Fighter Jet* to *Rocket* at the redline — while the gauge sweeps through the heat spectrum, a comet races around the ring, sparks fly, embers rise and every finished response sends out a shockwave. Beat your daily peak and it celebrates.
-- **Five orb styles, as many orbs as you like** — *LED Gauge*, *Needle Tachometer*, *Liquid Energy*, *Reactor* and *Minimal Ring*. Give each orb its own mix of sources (all of them, one tool, or Claude Code + Codex) and a glass name plate that stays legible on any wallpaper.
+- **Five orb styles, as many orbs as you like** — *LED Gauge*, *Needle Tachometer*, *Liquid Energy*, *Reactor* and *Minimal Ring*. Give each orb its own mix of source types and independently enable or disable each local or SSH host's sources. New sources are enabled by default; choices for disconnected hosts are retained. When hosts are excluded, peaks use observations of the selected sources rather than an unrelated historical peak. Each orb also has a glass name plate that stays legible on any wallpaper.
 - **Menu bar / taskbar** — a compact gauge and number that never jitters, right where you look: tok/s, money, or tok/s with the live money rate over today's total, plus optional network speed. On Windows it lives inside the taskbar, next to the clock.
 - **Dashboard** — a glowing line drawing of your current speed title's vehicle moves inside its orb — a walker, a bicycle pushing off, all the way to a rocket at the redline — plus a live chart, per-source speed, every active agent (including sub-agents) with its phase, and today's totals. Click a source to open its history.
 - **Performance score** — a benchmark-style number for every agent's live setup, where 1000 is the reference and there is no upper limit: higher is faster. It combines output throughput, time to first content, thinking speed, tool pace, tool time, tool success and cache hits, and compares it with the same model's usual on your computer (the 14 days before today). It shows on the orbs, the leaderboard boards, the menu bar / taskbar and the dashboard (hover for the breakdown), and the usage history charts each model's daily trend.
@@ -115,6 +115,14 @@ and use noninteractive key or SSH agent authentication. Enable each host in Sett
 enabled remote sources appear together in the native dashboard; source identity includes the host and source kind.
 On Windows, local source switches do not filter remote sources. Orb host/source exclusions are independent, so
 excluding a source on one host does not exclude the same source on another host.
+The orb source editor includes alternate connections to the same machine, so every connection that can
+contribute data can be selected independently. Duplicate host names are disambiguated by their connection.
+A dashboard opened from an orb follows that orb's current selection immediately, including its sources,
+agents and associated readings; changing the selection does not wait for another sample. Global dashboard
+entries remain global. Removing or hiding the associated orb closes its dashboard instead of silently
+switching to all sources.
+Orb and leaderboard live and daily values use missing placeholders when the selected remote data is incomplete,
+rather than displaying a partial sum as a complete value.
